---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About the project · LOLBAS">
  <section class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">COMMUNITY RESEARCH. SHARED KNOWLEDGE.</p>
    <h1>
      Nothing to LOL about<span class="brand-dot">.</span>
    </h1>
    <p>
      Living Off The Land Binaries, Scripts and Libraries. A community effort to
      document the unexpected capabilities of trusted Windows tools.
    </p>
  </section>
  <article class="article">
    <h2>The goal</h2>
    <p>
      Document every Microsoft-signed binary, script, and library that can be
      used for living off the land techniques. Legitimate tools can execute
      code, transfer files, bypass application allowlisting, access credentials,
      and perform other actions beyond their expected use.
    </p>
    <h2>What belongs in LOLBAS?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        A Microsoft-signed file, native to Windows or available from Microsoft.
      </li>
      <li>
        Unexpected functionality, with an exception for application allowlisting
        bypasses.
      </li>
      <li>
        Functionality useful in adversary simulation or to an advanced threat
        actor.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Read the{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS#criteria">
        full criteria
      </a>{' '}
      before submitting a finding.
    </p>
    <h2>Built by the community</h2>
    <p>
      The phrase “living off the land” was coined by Christopher Campbell and
      Matt Graeber at DerbyCon 3. LOLBAS grew from community research into a
      shared catalog maintained by volunteers.
    </p>
    <p>
      Project maintainers include Oddvar Moe, Jimmy Bayne, Conor Richard, Chris
      “Lopi” Spehn, Liam, Wietze, and Jose Hernandez. The original project logos
      were created by Adam Nadrowski.
    </p>
    <h2>Add your finding</h2>
    <p>
      Start with the{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md">
        contribution guide
      </a>{' '}
      and{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS/blob/master/YML-Template.yml">
        YAML template
      </a>
      . The original source format remains unchanged.
    </p>
    <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS">
      Explore the repository ↗
    </a>
    <h2>Keep exploring</h2>
    <p>
      For Unix binaries, visit{' '}
      <a href="https://gtfobins.github.io/">GTFOBins</a>. For Windows drivers,
      visit <a href="https://www.loldrivers.io/">LOLDrivers</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS/blob/master/NOTICE.md">
        License &amp; attribution
      </a>{' '}
      ·{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS/issues">
        Report an issue
      </a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
